============================================================================================
LEMMA A (2-adic characterisation of the direction symbol)
============================================================================================
  d_n = 1  <=>  v2(m_n+1) >= 2  ;  a d=1 step sends v2(m+1) -> v2(m+1)-1 ;
  hence the MAXIMAL d=1 run from x has length exactly v2(x+1) - 1.
PASS  d_n=1 <=> v2(m_n+1)>=2, and the step decrements v2(m+1): all odd 3<=m0<=60001, n<12 (0 violations)
PASS  maximal d=1 run length = v2(x+1) - 1 exactly (0 violations)

============================================================================================
LEMMA B (the two run estimates)
============================================================================================
  u consecutive d=1 steps:   y+1 = 3^u (x+1)/2^u   (EXACT), needs 2^u | x+1;
    for the run to be realisable at all, 2^{u+1} | x+1, so x >= 2^{u+1}-1.
  v consecutive d>=2 steps:  y-1 <= (3/4)^v (x-1), with equality stalling at x=1.
PASS  y+1 = 3^u(x+1)/2^u exact on every maximal leading ones-run (0)
PASS  2^{u+1} | x+1 for a maximal ones-run of length u (0)
PASS  y-1 <= (3/4)^v (x-1) on every maximal twos-run with states > 1 (0)

============================================================================================
THEOREM C (chained fixed-turn lifetime bound) -- derived, and the brief's
candidate F(k) = O((k+1) alpha^{k+1}) CORRECTED
============================================================================================
  Write h = log2(m+1), phi = log2(3/2) = alpha-1, psi = log2(4/3) = 2-alpha,
  so phi + psi = 1 and 1 + phi = alpha.  A ones-run of length u sends h -> h + u phi
  EXACTLY.  A twos-run of length v sends h -> h' with h' <= h - v psi + 1, using
  m-1 <= m+1 <= 2(m-1) for m >= 3.  With u_i <= h_i - 1 (Lemma A) and v_i >= 1,

        h_{i+1} <= h_i + (h_i - 1) phi - psi + 1 = alpha h_i ,

  so h_i <= alpha^{i-1} L with L = log2(m_0+1), and for j ones-runs

        sum u_i <= L (alpha^j - 1)/(alpha - 1) - j .

  Staying above m = 1 forces (sum v_i) psi <= L + (sum u_i) phi + j' - 1, and since
  1 + phi/psi = 1/psi,

        N  <=  (1/psi) [ sum u_i + L + j' - 1 ]
            <=  (L/(2-alpha)) * (alpha^j + alpha - 2)/(alpha - 1) ,      (*)

  with j = #ones-runs <= ceil((k+1)/2) and j' = #twos-runs.  So

        F(k) = Theta( alpha^{ceil((k+1)/2)} ) ,   NOT  O((k+1) alpha^{k+1}) :
  only the ones-runs compound, and there are about k/2 of them.  The brief's
  candidate overshoots by a factor about (k+1) alpha^{(k+1)/2}.
  coefficient of L in (*):  j=1 -> 4.818842   j=2 -> 8.637683   j=3 -> 14.690404   j=5 -> 39.488817

  SHARPNESS at j=1.  A Mersenne seed 2^{u+1}-1 does exactly u ones-steps first,
  but its orbit generally starts FURTHER ones-runs before reaching 1, so j > 1
  and the j=1 bound does not apply to it.  (An earlier version of this panel
